Pass native local paths to a UNICODE StormLib

StormLib takes local file names as TCHAR strings, which on Windows are wide
when it is built with UNICODE -- and this repository builds it that way from
stormlib 9.40-3 on. Its CMake target then exports STORMLIB_UNICODE, and
StormLib.h rejects a consumer compiled without UNICODE. mpqcli therefore
builds with UNICODE and _UNICODE whenever the StormLib it finds is a UNICODE
one, and exactly as before otherwise.

The seven places that hand StormLib a local path go through two helpers
instead of passing std::string::c_str() straight through:

  - StormArgPath() for paths typed on the command line. They reach main() in
    the ANSI code page, so they are converted with CP_ACP -- what the ANSI
    StormLib's CreateFileA did internally, so any path that opened before
    still opens. std::filesystem::path cannot do this conversion portably:
    built from a narrow string, libstdc++ decodes it as UTF-8 and libc++ as
    ANSI.

  - StormFsPath() for paths that already are std::filesystem::path objects
    (the directory walk behind "add", the resolved destination of
    "extract"). Those were flattened with u8string() and handed to the ANSI
    API as if they were in the ANSI code page, which garbled any non-ASCII
    name; a UNICODE build now passes the native wide path.

Without a UNICODE StormLib -- other platforms, or an ANSI build on Windows --
both helpers return exactly what was passed before.

Upstream: not submitted yet
Applies-to: all environments

--- a/src/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/src/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -44,6 +44,14 @@
 # Link libraries
 target_link_libraries(mpqcli PRIVATE StormLib::storm CLI11::CLI11)
 
+# StormLib takes local file names as TCHAR strings. A UNICODE build exports
+# STORMLIB_UNICODE, and StormLib.h rejects a consumer compiled for the other
+# flavour, so build for whichever one was found.
+get_target_property(STORMLIB_DEFINITIONS StormLib::storm INTERFACE_COMPILE_DEFINITIONS)
+if (WIN32 AND "STORMLIB_UNICODE" IN_LIST STORMLIB_DEFINITIONS)
+    target_compile_definitions(mpqcli PRIVATE UNICODE _UNICODE)
+endif()
+
 # Install
 include(GNUInstallDirs)
 install(TARGETS mpqcli RUNTIME DESTINATION ${CMAKE_INSTALL_BINDIR})
